evidence.quote:
If M is an aspherical closed manifold of even dimension, then
(−1)dim(M)/2 · χ(M) ≥ 0.

If M is a closed Riemannian manifold of even dimension with sectional curvature sec(M), then
(−1)dim(M)/2 · χ(M) > 0 if sec(M) < 0;
(−1)dim(M)/2 · χ(M) ≥ 0 if sec(M) ≤ 0;
χ(M) ≥ 0 if sec(M) ≥ 0;
χ(M) > 0 if sec(M) > 0.

artifact.self_contained_problem:
A closed manifold M is called aspherical if its universal cover is contractible (equivalently, π_k(M)=0 for all k≥2). Let χ(M) denote the Euler characteristic of M and, for a Riemannian metric, let sec(M) denote its sectional curvature.

(a) (Aspherical version.) Prove or disprove: if M is an aspherical closed manifold of even dimension, then
   (−1)^{dim(M)/2} · χ(M) ≥ 0.

(b) (Curvature version.) Prove or disprove the following statements for every closed Riemannian manifold M of even dimension:
   (i)   if sec(M) < 0 everywhere, then (−1)^{dim(M)/2} · χ(M) > 0;
   (ii)  if sec(M) ≤ 0 everywhere, then (−1)^{dim(M)/2} · χ(M) ≥ 0;
   (iii) if sec(M) ≥ 0 everywhere, then χ(M) ≥ 0;
   (iv)  if sec(M) > 0 everywhere, then χ(M) > 0.

